// Package recs is the pure recommendation score model
// (recommendation-sorting D2/D6): one additive score per browsable video
// entity, derived at read time and never persisted —
//
//	score(e) = 1000·inProgress + 500·newEpisode + min(Σ weight(t), 400)
//
// with weight(t) = 1 + interest(t), interest starting at zero. The tier
// constants pin the user's ordering rule: any tag affinity ranks below a
// new episode (500), which ranks below a resume point (1000) — context
// always dominates affinity, and bonuses stack. Equal scores tie-break by
// the served display name ascending, then id — the alphabetical floor.
//
// The package is a pure leaf: it imports nothing from mellifera and takes
// plain input structs (context facts, tag lists, interest weights). The
// api composes — batched store reads fill an EntityState, Score returns
// the number, Order sorts the served surface. Zero interest degrades to
// today's order: every score is the tag base sum and the grid falls back
// to alphabetical.
//
// # Public API (6 symbols — the ≤8 ceiling holds)
//
//   - Score: the one score function over an EntityState and interest
//     Weights.
//
//   - EntityState: the context facts (in-progress, new-episode) plus the
//     entity's tag list, verbatim from the winning document.
//
//   - Weights: learned interest per normalized tag key; missing keys are
//     the base.
//
//   - NormalizeTag: the one tag-key normalization (trim + Unicode
//     casefold) every weight read and write passes through.
//
//   - Entry, Order: the served-surface row and its sort — score desc,
//     display name asc, id asc.
//
// The tier constants are exported read-only for composition sites and
// tests: BonusInProgress (1000), BonusNewEpisode (500), TagCap (400).
